  "prediction": "**Deadly Shooting on Las Vegas Strip Leaves Three Dead and Six Injured**\n\nA deadly shooting on the Las Vegas Strip early Thursday morning left three people dead and at least six injured. The incident occurred when a black Range Rover opened fire on a Maserati, causing it to crash into a taxi that burst into flames. The taxi driver and passenger were killed, along with the driver of the Maserati. The passenger in the Maserati was shot and taken to the hospital for treatment.\n\n**Investigation Underway**\n\nPolice are investigating the incident, which they believe was sparked by an altercation at a nearby casino resort. The Range Rover, which had tinted windows and paper dealer plates, fled the scene and was last seen near the Venetian hotel. Police have contacted authorities in three neighboring states to be on the lookout for the vehicle.\n\n**Victims Identified**\n\nThe driver of the Maserati, Kenneth Wayne Cherry Jr., 27, was identified as one of the victims. He was an aspiring rapper and had a reputation for driving a Maserati on the Strip. The taxi driver, Michael Boldon, was also identified as a victim. He had recently moved to Las Vegas to care for his 93-year-old mother.\n\n**Eyewitness Accounts**\n\nEyewitnesses described the scene as chaotic, with multiple vehicles involved in the crash and fire. One witness, Eric Lackey, took a photo of the burning taxi and described the scene as \"something out of a movie.\" Another witness, Mark Thompson, said he was visiting from England and was shocked by the violence.\n\n**Police Response**\n\nPolice have video from traffic cameras at the intersection and are checking hotel surveillance systems to determine the cause of the altercation. They have also identified several people who were in the Range Rover, but have not released their names.\n\n**Recent Violence on the Strip**\n\nThe incident marks the latest in a series of violent incidents on the Las Vegas Strip. In recent weeks, there have been two other shootings, including one at a parking garage and another in an elevator at The Hotel at Mandalay Bay. Police have made arrests or identified suspects in each case.\n\n**Tourist Reaction**\n\nDespite the violence, many tourists expressed confidence in the safety of the Strip. \"Las Vegas is one of the safest cities in the world,\" said Jeremy Handel, a spokesman for the Las Vegas Convention and Visitors Authority. \"We have advanced technology and training to keep our visitors safe.\"\n\nHowever, others were more skeptical. \"It's the wild west out here,\" said Paul",
